        ":question/problem": "Calculate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int\\frac{4\\ln x}{x}dx$.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's set $u=\\ln{\\left(x \\right)}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =4\\int \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{u^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =2 u^{2}+C \\\\  & =2 \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
